    {
      "id": "goge7i1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.1 General Climate"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Odisha has a tropical monsoon climate, characterized by hot and humid summers, heavy monsoon rainfall, and mild winters. The Bay of Bengal's proximity causes high humidity throughout the year and makes the state prone to cyclones.",
      "id": "5gqdm4z"
    },
    {
      "id": "selevj9",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Season</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Period &amp; Features</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Summer</p>",
            "<p>March to May; hot and humid; max temp 40–45°C in interior</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>South-West Monsoon</p>",
            "<p>June to September; heavy rainfall; 80% of annual rain in this period</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Post-Monsoon</p>",
            "<p>October–November; retreating monsoon; cyclone season</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Winter</p>",
            "<p>December to February; cool and dry; mild along coast</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "zkkggi6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.2 Rainfall"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Odisha receives average annual rainfall of 1,489 mm. Distribution varies significantly across regions:",
      "id": "fskvrhs"
    },
    {
      "id": "inmmcej",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Region</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Rainfall (Annual)</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Districts</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Highest Rainfall</p>",
            "<p>&gt;2000 mm</p>",
            "<p>Koraput, Malkangiri, Nabarangapur, Mayurbhanj</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Heavy Rainfall</p>",
            "<p>1400-2000 mm</p>",
            "<p>Puri, Cuttack, Keonjhar, Sundargarh</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Moderate Rainfall</p>",
            "<p>1000-1400 mm</p>",
            "<p>Bolangir, Bargarh, Sambalpur</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Lowest Rainfall</p>",
            "<p>&lt;1000 mm</p>",
            "<p>Nuapada, parts of Kalahandi</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "85i9zlh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.3 Cyclones"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Odisha is highly vulnerable to tropical cyclones from the Bay of Bengal. Major cyclones that devastated Odisha:",
      "id": "dlud6vw"
    },
    {
      "id": "xwicl2a",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Cyclone</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Year</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Impact</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Super Cyclone</p>",
            "<p>1999</p>",
            "<p>Most devastating; 15,000+ deaths; Paradip severely hit</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Phailin</p>",
            "<p>2013</p>",
            "<p>Very severe; effective evacuation saved lives</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hudhud</p>",
            "<p>2014</p>",
            "<p>Hit Andhra; affected Odisha coast</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Titli</p>",
            "<p>2018</p>",
            "<p>Ganjam, Gajapati; heavy casualties</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Fani (Category 4)</p>",
            "<p>2019</p>",
            "<p>Extremely severe; mass evacuation (1.2 million people); Puri hit directly</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Amphan</p>",
            "<p>2020</p>",
            "<p>Affected coastal Odisha</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Yaas</p>",
            "<p>2021</p>",
            "<p>Balasore, Bhadrak severely affected</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "enriched": false
}